From 3fd18662daf67e4b86e9b18d838c08fc45d427dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Faure <david.faure@kdab.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 15:03:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] QMimeDatabase: fix parsing of hex escapes in magic values
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

makePattern consumed the character after a one-digit hex escape such as
\xa even when it wasn't a hex digit. shared-mime-info 2.5 uses
"\xa\x0\x0\x0MSWordDoc\x0" for application/msword, which turned into a
newline followed by the literal "x0", so the rule never matched.
Only consume hex digits, and treat \x without any digit as a literal
'x', like update-mime-database does, so that the XML and cache
providers agree.

Pick-to: 6.11
Change-Id: I05d558c104810e0fa956d036cee3ad4de42ba849
Reviewed-by: Mårten Nordheim <marten.nordheim@qt.io>
Reviewed-by: Tatiana Borisova <tatiana.borisova@qt.io>
(cherry picked from commit 3b4383877b8e65051bb6ea9e1a1304f531257c0d)
Reviewed-by: Qt Cherry-pick Bot <cherrypick_bot@qt-project.org>
Origin: upstream, https://invent.kde.org/qt/qt/qtbase/-/commit/3fd18662daf67e4b86e9b18d838c08fc45d427dc
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-29
